// expect: 42
// A PARAMETER NAMED LIKE A STRUCTURAL LEAF IS HIJACKED. `hash` here is
// `apply`'s own parameter, bound to `inc`, so `hash(x)` is 42. The program
// answers 41: lowering intercepts every call spelled `hash` and emits the
// structural hash leaf instead of calling the parameter (measured
// 2026-09-25; `mentl check` is clean). Renaming the parameter answers 42.
//
// Retires when lowering recognizes the leaf by the declaration a call
// resolves to, never by its spelling (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
fn apply(hash, x) = hash(x)

fn inc(n) = n + 1

fn main() = apply(inc, 41)
